  ('What Your Kitchen Table Says About You', 'what-your-kitchen-table-says-about-you', 'A tour of six tables and the lives that happen around them.', '<p>There is a particular kind of quiet that only arrives when you stop trying to fill it. There were setbacks, of course. Plans changed, budgets ran out, the weather refused to cooperate. But every obstacle seemed to sharpen the purpose rather than blunt it.</p><p>It would be easy to make this a story about nostalgia, but that isn''t quite right. It is a story about attention — about choosing what to notice and then noticing it properly.</p><h2>Why it matters</h2><p>What struck me most was how ordinary it all seemed from the outside, and how extraordinary it felt once I was part of it. The people involved never described what they did as remarkable; to them it was simply Tuesday. What struck me most was how ordinary it all seemed from the outside, and how extraordinary it felt once I was part of it. The people involved never described what they did as remarkable; to them it was simply Tuesday.</p><blockquote><p>You don''t find the time. You take it, and then you protect it like it''s the last of something.</p></blockquote><p>The details matter here: the smell of the place, the sound of footsteps on old floors, the way conversations drift and return. These are the things you can''t plan for and can''t fake.</p><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/byb-inline-7/1200/700" alt=""><h2>The hard part</h2><p>What struck me most was how ordinary it all seemed from the outside, and how extraordinary it felt once I was part of it. The people involved never described what they did as remarkable; to them it was simply Tuesday. Whether it lasts is almost beside the point. It is here now, and that is enough.</p>', 'https://picsum.photos/seed/byb-what-your-kitchen-table-says-about-you/1600/1000', (select id from public.categories where slug = 'style'), (select id from admin_user), 'magazine', 'published', false, now() - interval '15 days 3 hours'),
