  ('The Market That Opens at Four in the Morning', 'the-market-that-opens-at-four-in-the-morning', 'Fishmongers, florists and the best coffee in the city, before the city wakes.', '<p>There is a particular kind of quiet that only arrives when you stop trying to fill it. It would be easy to make this a story about nostalgia, but that isn''t quite right. It is a story about attention — about choosing what to notice and then noticing it properly.</p><p>It would be easy to make this a story about nostalgia, but that isn''t quite right. It is a story about attention — about choosing what to notice and then noticing it properly.</p><h2>The people</h2><p>It would be easy to make this a story about nostalgia, but that isn''t quite right. It is a story about attention — about choosing what to notice and then noticing it properly. There were setbacks, of course. Plans changed, budgets ran out, the weather refused to cooperate. But every obstacle seemed to sharpen the purpose rather than blunt it.</p><blockquote><p>Once you''ve seen it done properly, you can''t go back to doing it badly.</p></blockquote><p>What struck me most was how ordinary it all seemed from the outside, and how extraordinary it felt once I was part of it. The people involved never described what they did as remarkable; to them it was simply Tuesday.</p><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/byb-inline-16/1200/700" alt=""><h2>Looking ahead</h2><p>The economics don''t make sense on paper. They rarely do. And yet here it is, thriving in a way that spreadsheets can''t explain. Maybe that is the lesson: commit, and let the rest follow.</p>', 'https://picsum.photos/seed/byb-the-market-that-opens-at-four-in-the-morning/1600/1000', (select id from public.categories where slug = 'travel'), (select id from admin_user), 'magazine', 'published', false, now() - interval '32 days 19 hours'),
  ('Walking the Coast Path in Winter', 'walking-the-coast-path-in-winter', 'Empty beaches, closed cafés and a sea that looks like slate.', '<p>Ask anyone who has done it, and they will tell you the hardest part was the first step. It would be easy to make this a story about nostalgia, but that isn''t quite right. It is a story about attention — about choosing what to notice and then noticing it properly.</p><p>The details matter here: the smell of the place, the sound of footsteps on old floors, the way conversations drift and return. These are the things you can''t plan for and can''t fake.</p><h2>The people</h2><p>The details matter here: the smell of the place, the sound of footsteps on old floors, the way conversations drift and return. These are the things you can''t plan for and can''t fake. There were setbacks, of course. Plans changed, budgets ran out, the weather refused to cooperate. But every obstacle seemed to sharpen the purpose rather than blunt it.</p><blockquote><p>We''re not trying to be the biggest. We''re trying to still be here in twenty years.</p></blockquote><p>What struck me most was how ordinary it all seemed from the outside, and how extraordinary it felt once I was part of it. The people involved never described what they did as remarkable; to them it was simply Tuesday.</p><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/byb-inline-17/1200/700" alt=""><h2>How it began</h2><p>There were setbacks, of course. Plans changed, budgets ran out, the weather refused to cooperate. But every obstacle seemed to sharpen the purpose rather than blunt it. I''ll be going back. I suspect you will too, once you''ve been once.</p>', 'https://picsum.photos/seed/byb-walking-the-coast-path-in-winter/1600/1000', (select id from public.categories where slug = 'travel'), (select id from admin_user), 'magazine', 'published', false, now() - interval '35 days 18 hours'),
